e>Situ</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Wei</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Mashhoon</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bobek</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human salivary MUC7 mucin peptides: effect of size, charge and cysteine residues on antifungal activity</article-title><source>Biochem J</source><year>2003</year><volume>375</volume><fpage>175</fpage><lpage>182</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12812519</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1042/BJ20030779</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wei</surname><given-names>GX</given-names></name><name><surname>Bobek</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>In vitro synergic antifungal effect of MUC7 12-mer with histatin-5 12-mer or miconazole</article-title><source>J Antimicrob Chemother</source><year>2004</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>750</fpage><lpage>758</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15073161</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/jac/dkh181</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wei</surname><given-names>GX</given-names></name><name><surname>Bobek</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human salivary mucin MUC7 12-mer-L and 12-mer-D peptides: antifungal activity in saliva, enhancement of activity with protease inhibitor cocktail or EDTA, and cytotoxicity to human cells</article-title><source>Antimicrob Agents Chemother</source><year>2005</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>2336</fpage><lpage>2342</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15917530</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/AAC.49.6.2336-2342.2005</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><perso